{
  "file": "crates/trust-but-verify/tests/storage.rs",
  "item": "impl[StoredGraph/Domain]/fn[node_content]",
  "citations": [
    {
      "role": "cite",
      "name": "habeas:coverage",
      "commentary": "This storage-only consumer must delegate load/store using node_path\n without resolving contents. Domain requires the callback, but invoking\n this guard would violate the no-content-read invariant of the test.\n Other graph fixtures exercise content resolution."
    }
  ],
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The `habeas:coverage` citation on `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/storage.rs#impl[StoredGraph/Domain]/fn[node_content]` is appropriate.\n\n- **Form:** The citation is a fenced commentary block on an explicit function with a body. That is the form `habeas:coverage` allows for excusing a function's zero execution.\n- **The reason is substantive.** The function is a deliberate `panic!` guard. The fixture is meant to prove that storage operations never resolve node contents, so executing the guard would fail the test. That is a real reason, not just difficulty in covering the code.\n- **The claims match the source.**\n  - `Domain::node_content` in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/domain.rs` has no default body, so `StoredGraph` has to implement it.\n  - The fixture's `node_path` builds the storage path from the node. Its `NodeContent` type is the uninhabited `UnreadContents`.\n  - The storage tests, `consumer_delegates_evidence_storage_using_only_the_requested_nodes_path` and `malformed_records_are_storage_errors_and_bad_outputs_are_output_errors`, only load and store evidence. The record they reload comes from a `StoredReview` that reads no nodes, so it has no `Dependency::Node` entries. That means `dependencies_are_current` in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/graph.rs` would not call `node_content` for it.\n- **Other fixtures cover content resolution.** The reference to other graph fixtures is supported by the `node_content` implementations in `src/agent/tests.rs` (`Memory`) and `src/agent/project_sources.rs` (`Project`), which do read contents.\n- **No redundancy:** The item carries no `{impl}` or `{test}` reference to the same target, so the citation is not redundant.",
